{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966813,"nonce":"flGfF//11HBqWpDOIifzH9gsr8g=","title":"Deferred DSL bodies resolve FSM context through a captured handler context; the scope","message":"Landed 2026-08-14 on `wip/fsm-machine-scope`. A `computed`, `effect`,\n`on_click` or fsm subscriber captures the handler context in force\nwhere it was written (`deferred_ctx::Deferred`) and reinstates it when\nit runs. The scope bracket installs its component's machine handlers\nfor the WHOLE view body, which is what makes those captures non-empty.\nA context read asks the installed handler first and falls back to the\nscope lookup only when there is none.\n\nProven, not assumed: with scope re-entry for deferred bodies disabled\nentirely, the suite stays green, so the handler path is what answers.\n\n**DONE 2026-08-15: the ambient scope is gone.** Reads resolve through\nthe installed handler, triggers through the installed machine list, and\n`__blinc_fsm_ensure__` takes the mount id as an argument. The three\nsites that were left asking `current_scope()` all measured as scope 0,\nso they now name `NO_SCOPE` outright. `scope.rs` is that one constant;\nthe bracket is `__blinc_fsm_mount_enter__` / `_leave__` and installs\nmachines for the extent of a view body.\n\n**Correction to the earlier plan:** machines are ALREADY keyed on mount\nidentity. The scope value is literally `__instance_id__`, the\nper-call-site key `inject_call_site_keys` bakes -- measured, not\nassumed: the bracket receives a large stable nonzero id, the same one\nacross renders of a mount, never 0. So `by_key` is `(mount, fsm)` and\nthere is no re-keying work to do.\n\nWhat is left of the scope layer is only the AMBIENT part, the\nthread-local `CURRENT`, with three readers:\n\n- the read fallback, which goes when the fallback does,\n- `blinc_fsm_ensure`, which reads `current_scope()` instead of taking\n  the instance id it could be handed (a signature change, nothing more),\n- `step_machine`, which is the real one: it decides which instance a\n  `dispatch_default` drives. Routing a dispatch through the installed\n  handler instead is what actually retires `scope.rs`, and it is also\n  what would let a test drive a component's own machine (see the\n  isolation-only assertion in `deferred_context_read.rs`).\n\n**The name-keyed fallback** (`mangle_ctx_signal` + the baked id) was\nnever taken on any path that calls `__blinc_fsm_ctx_id__` across the\nsuite. Not the same as unused: `with_blocks`' FSM region never calls\nthat extern at all, so its reads resolve some other way. Establish what\nthat path is before retiring the fallback.\n\nSee gotcha fsm read must not create for why reads never construct,\nand gotcha fsm scope bracket any type for the bracket bug that hid\nall of this.","files":null}]}